  "verbalization": "Mutongsaponin B is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to the cell line FaDu. The evidence suggests that Mutongsaponin B interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in epigenetic regulation. This complex is targeted by a compound with the structure described, which is itself a known inhibitor of the PRC2 complex. The interaction with this complex may affect gene expression patterns in FaDu cells, potentially leading to cellular changes that could influence the behavior of the cell line.\n\nAdditionally, Mutongsaponin B is also shown to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is a target of Alpha-Humulene Epoxide. This pathway may contribute to the observed effects on FaDu cells, though the specific mechanism is not fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets, including both epigenetic and enzymatic pathways, suggests a multifaceted interaction that could influence the biological processes in FaDu cells.\n\nThe evidence is consistent with the possibility that Mutongsaponin B exerts its effects on FaDu cells through a combination of mechanisms, including modulation of epigenetic regulation and enzymatic activity. However, the exact nature of these interactions and their contribution to the observed effects on FaDu cells remains to be fully characterized. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Mutongsaponin B and FaDu, emphasizing the need for further experimental validation to understand the precise mechanisms involved.",
